This product includes a modified fork of image-webp from the image-rs project,
licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0. The fork branches from image-rs/image-webp at
commit f4d80bd (after the 0.2.4 release) and adds seventeen commits: a VP8 lossy
still-image encoder — per-macroblock intra prediction chosen by rate-distortion
cost, coefficient-free macroblock skipping, a nonlinear quality-to-quantizer
curve, and quantizer-proportional loop filtering — alongside lossless encoder,
decoder, and animation fixes. On top of those, the fork keeps nanoraster's
deterministic Huffman tie-break, which holds lossless output identical between
32-bit and 64-bit targets. Its source and license text are retained under
rust/vendor/image-webp/.

This product includes wgpu-hal 30.0.0 from the gfx-rs/wgpu project, licensed
under MIT OR Apache-2.0, with one nanoraster patch: Direct3D 12 pipeline state
stream subobjects are aligned to the pointer size rather than to eight bytes,
which lets the DX12 backend create pipelines on 32-bit Windows. Its source and
license text are retained under rust/vendor/wgpu-hal/.
